\section{Final No-Tuning Closure (Option 1)}
% ============================================================

\subsection{Unified statement}
\begin{enumerate}[label=\arabic*)]
\item \textbf{Scale invariance}: with $m(\aL)=\rhozero\aL^3$ and $k(\aL)=\Szero\aL$, any signal speed derived from $\C^2\propto (k/m)\aL^2$ becomes independent of $\aL$:
\[
\frac{k(\aL)}{m(\aL)}\aL^2 = \frac{\Szero\aL}{\rhozero\aL^3}\aL^2=\frac{\Szero}{\rhozero}.
\]
\item \textbf{Void/jamming switch}: $\phi$ does not tune $\C$ continuously by $1/\sqrt{\phi}$; rather, $\phi$ decides whether a spanning contact network exists (hence whether $B_{\mathrm{eff}}$ is zero or not).
\item \textbf{Point-J factor unity}: at jamming, $Z\to 6$ (backbone, frictionless 3D), giving $\GammaS_J=1$ in the scalar propagation model.
\end{enumerate}

\subsection{The final formula}
Thus, at the Level-0 critical state (Point-J),
\begin{equation}
\boxed{\;\C^2=\frac{\Szero}{\rhozero}\;}
\end{equation}
with $\C$ a Level-0 fundamental constant (Option 1). Geometry/jamming provides a no-tuning explanation for why extraneous factors (lattice size $\aL$, packing fraction $\phi$) drop out or become structurally fixed.

